$$3$$4$$2$$v_{1}$$v_{2}$$v_{3}$$v_{4}$$v_{5}$$v_{6}$$v_{1}$$-$$-$$10$$-$$6$$3$$v_{2}$$-$$-$$8$$9$$-$$4$$v_{3}$$10$$8$$-$$19$$-$$-$$v_{4}$$-$$9$$19$$-$$-$$7$$v_{5}$$6$$-$$-$$-$$-$$-$$v_{6}$$3$$4$$-$$7$$-$$-$ | Added edgesLength$v_{1} - v_{6}$$3$$v_{6} - v_{2}$$4$$v_{1} - v_{5}$$6$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} $…$$…$ |\n| --- | ---: |"}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying One Iteration of Prim's Algorithm Using a Distance Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110681 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110367 :question/id #uuid "6eba4b87-8735-54c0-8552-f76f516ada6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-16371" :question/problem "|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | $v_1$ | $v_2$ | $v_3$ | $v_4$ | $v_5$ | $v_6$ |\n| $v_1$ | $-$ | $10$ | $-$ | $3$ | $-$ | $12$ |\n| $v_2$ | $10$ | $-$ | $7$ | $-$ | $8$ | $-$ |\n| $v_3$ | $-$ | $7$ | $-$ | $-$ | $15$ | $6$ |\n| $v_4$ | $3$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $v_5$ | $-$ | $8$ | $15$ | $-$ | $-$ | $2$ |\n| $v_6$ | $12$ | $-$ | $6$ | $-$ | $2$ | $-$ |\n\nConsider the distance matrix of a weighted graph shown above. Using Prim's algorithm starting from the vertex $v_1$, find a minimum spanning tree of this graph." :question/worked-solution "The pseudocode for Prim's algorithm on a distance matrix is the following:\n\n> `Mark the column corresponding to the starting vertex`\n> `Cancel out the row corresponding to the starting vertex`\n> `while (not all columns are marked):`\n> `Find the smallest distance s over all the marked columns`\n> `Let u and v be the row and column corresponding to s`\n> `Mark the column u corresponding to s`\n> `Cancel out the row u corresponding to s`\n> `Add edge v-u to the tree`\n\nWith that in mind, we proceed as follows:\n\n| **Step 1.** Mark column $v_1$ and cancel out row $v_1$. |  |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1$$v_1$$v_2$$v_3$$v_4$$v_5$$v_6$$v_1$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}12$$v_2$$10$$-$$7$$-$$8$$-$$v_3$$-$$7$$-$$-$$15$$6$$v_4$$3$$-$$-$$-$$-$$-$$v_5$$-$$8$$15$$-$$-$$2$$v_6$$12$$-$$6$$-$$2$$-$ | Added edgesLength |\n| **Step 2.** The smallest unselected value in the marked column is $3$ located at the intersection of row $v_4$ and column $v_1$. So, we mark column $v_4$, cancel out row $v_4$, and add edge $v_1-v_4$ to the tree. |  |\n| $1$$2$$v_1$$v_2$$v_3$$v_4$$v_5$$v_6$$v_1$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}12$$v_2$$10$$-$$7$$-$$8$$-$$v_3$$-$$7$$-$$-$$15$$6$$v_4$$3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$v_5$$-$$8$$15$$-$$-$$2$$v_6$$12$$-$$6$$-$$2$$-$ | Added edgesLength$v_1 - v_4$$3$ |\n| **Step 3.** The smallest unselected value in the marked columns is $10$ located at the intersection of row $v_2$ and column $v_1$. So, we mark column $v_2$, cancel out row $v_2$, and add edge $v_1-v_2$ to the tree. |  |\n| $1$$3$$2$$v_1$$v_2$$v_3$$v_4$$v_5$$v_6$$v_1$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}12$$v_2$$10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}7$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}8$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$v_3$$-$$7$$-$$-$$15$$6$$v_4$$3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$v_5$$-$$8$$15$$-$$-$$2$$v_6$$12$$-$$6$$-$$2$$-$ | Added edgesLength$v_1 - v_4$$3$$v_1 - v_2$$10$ |\n| **Step 4.** The smallest unselected value in the marked columns is $7$ located at the intersection of row $v_3$ and column $v_2$. So, we mark column $v_3$, cancel out row $v_3$, and add edge $v_2-v_3$ to the tree. |  |\n| $1$$3$$4$$2$$v_1$$v_2$$v_3$$v_4$$v_5$$v_6$$v_1$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}12$$v_2$$10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}7$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}8$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$v_3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$7$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}15$$\\color{lightgrey}6$$v_4$$3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$v_5$$-$$8$$15$$-$$-$$2$$v_6$$12$$-$$6$$-$$2$$-$ | Added edgesLength$v_1 - v_4$$3$$v_1 - v_2$$10$$v_2 - v_3$$7$ |\n| **Step 5.** The smallest unselected value in the marked columns is $6$ located at the intersection of row $v_6$ and column $v_3$. So, we mark column $v_6$, cancel out row $v_6$, and add edge $v_3-v_6$ to the tree. |  |\n| $1$$3$$4$$2$$5$$v_1$$v_2$$v_3$$v_4$$v_5$$v_6$$v_1$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}12$$v_2$$10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}7$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}8$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$v_3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$7$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}15$$\\color{lightgrey}6$$v_4$$3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$v_5$$-$$8$$15$$-$$-$$2$$v_6$$\\color{lightgrey}12$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$6$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}2$$\\color{lightgrey}-$ | Added edgesLength$v_1 - v_4$$3$$v_1 - v_2$$10$$v_2 - v_3$$7$$v_3 - v_6$$6$ |\n| **Step 6.** The smallest unselected value in the marked columns is $2$ located at the intersection of row $v_5$ and column $v_6$. So, we mark column $v_5$, cancel out row $v_5$, and add edge $v_6-v_5$ to the tree. |  |\n| $1$$3$$4$$2$$6$$5$$v_1$$v_2$$v_3$$v_4$$v_5$$v_6$$v_1$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}12$$v_2$$10$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}7$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}8$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$v_3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$7$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}15$$\\color{lightgrey}6$$v_4$$3$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$v_5$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}8$$\\color{lightgrey}15$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$2$$v_6$$\\color{lightgrey}12$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$6$$\\color{lightgrey}-$$\\color{lightgrey}2$$\\color{lightgrey}-$ | Added edgesLength$v_1 - v_4$$3$$v_1 - v_2$$10$$v_2 - v_3$$7$$v_3 - v_6$$6$$v_6 - v_5$$2$ |\n\nThe total weight of the resulting minimum spanning tree is\n\n$$\n3 + 10 + 7 + 6 + 2 = 28\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "18104f56-26c0-5538-8e37-8aee8de0fd36" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a77ae0cb-240c-5060-b3e7-65b30596f6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108032} {:answer/id #uuid "b34688d0-2e15-5116-a63d-b1ce15e1943d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108033} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c9c95f-5aeb-5f71-9930-fce12b08d75b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108034} {:answer/id #uuid "46cb473d-223c-5029-aff6-80b0972aa238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108035} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff81a2a-79c7-5293-a391-887c799eef45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v_{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108036} {:answer/id #uuid "5c5d1228-7671-54a5-be6a-4f700fd13ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v_{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108037}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7749fdfb-826c-56ec-9585-adfbee4cb7f5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108031} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbb618af-9124-5ded-a85b-172ec841c119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108039} {:answer/id #