{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 13 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}47 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 19\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357686 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03a71052-5e5a-507b-8bda-885193362564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354686} {:answer/id #uuid "2be3bb07-6365-5037-b4b3-e11820f84cac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355037} {:answer/id #uuid "79c0a991-6850-5e2c-a589-9eb8a602cba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355731} {:answer/id #uuid "896fa9c9-4232-51c5-8120-eb24b94e0ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355881} {:answer/id #uuid "ec65c1ea-cb5e-52c5-b6ab-41489c7848b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end